UID:982667
DESCRIPTION:<p><em>Operation Mincemeat</em> is the 2024 Olivier Award-winn
 ing Best New Musical \, the 2025 Tony Award&reg\; winner for Best Featured
  Actor in a Musical (Jak Malone)\, and was named the #1 Broadway Show of 2
 025 (<em>Entertainment Weekly</em>).<br /><br />The year is 1943 and right
  now we&rsquo\;re losing the war. Luckily\, we&rsquo\;re about to gamble a
 ll our futures on a stolen corpse. Bursting at the seams with the kind of 
 chaos you couldn&rsquo\;t invent\, the question is: how did a dead body\, 
 a fake love letter\, and&mdash\;of all people&mdash\;Ian Fleming come toge
 ther to wrong-foot Hitler?<br /><br />&ldquo\;It's not just the best music
 al I&rsquo\;ve ever seen\; it&rsquo\;s the most rewarding theatrical exper
 ience I&rsquo\;ve ever had.&rdquo\; - Taffy Brodesser-Akner\, <em>The New 
 York Times Magazine</em><br /><br />&ldquo\;The reviews have been ecstatic
 . The overwhelming impression is of hopefulness\, possibility\, and joy.&r
 dquo\; &mdash\; <em>The New York Times</em><br /><br />&ldquo\;The Brits h
 ave made the year&rsquo\;s funniest musical.&rdquo\; &mdash\; Peter Marks\
 , <em>The Washington Post</em><br /><br />&ldquo\;The best new song on Bro
 adway&hellip\; that song will be sung for the next hundred years.&rdquo\; 
 &mdash\; <em>Vulture</em><br /><br />&ldquo\;Part Mel Brooks\, part <em>SI
 X</em>\, part <em>Hamilton</em> with a side order of <em>One Man\, Two Guv
 nors</em>.&rdquo\; &mdash\; <em>The Daily Mirror</em><br /><br />&ldquo\;T
 oo British? Not if you want to laugh uproariously &mdash\; and perhaps eve
 n unexpectedly shed a tear or two.&rdquo\; &mdash\; <em>Variety<br /><br /
 ></em>&ldquo\;A laugh-out-loud delight\, with endless charm&hellip\; There
 &rsquo\;s nothing else like it on Broadway.&rdquo\;  - <em>Entertainment W
 eekly</em></p>
LOCATION:Golden Theatre\, 252 West 45th Street\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
